WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.310
When Marvel's biggest film of 2018, the exhilarating
and surprisingly sad superhero ensemble Avengers:

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:10.140
Infinity War, hit Netflix on December 25th,
fans were delighted.

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:13.940
A Christmas present from the Home of Heroes
and the number-one streaming platform in the

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:14.440
world?

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:18.360
A chance to watch the super-sized flick in
their pajamas, sunk into the corner of their

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:22.610
couch and hiding behind a bowl of popcorn
where no one could judge them for crying when

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:26.480
Spider-Man said a tearful goodbye to Iron
Man in the last few minutes of the film?

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:28.320
Who wouldn't be excited by that?

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:33.360
Unfortunately, elation turned to outrage for
a vocal contingent of Marvel fans when Netflix

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:36.000
users discovered the Infinity War plot summary.

00:00:36.289 --> 00:00:40.719
At the time the film hit the streaming site,
its description read, "Superheroes amass to

00:00:40.719 --> 00:00:45.670
stop intergalactic sociopath Thanos from acquiring
a full set of Infinity Stones and wiping out

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:47.520
half of all life in the universe."

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:52.200
As it turns out, some concerned movie watchers
took issue with the use of the phrase "intergalactic

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:57.010
sociopath" to describe Thanos, the purple-faced
despot who committed mass genocide with the

00:00:57.010 --> 00:00:59.520
snap of his Infinity Gauntlet-adorned fingers.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:03.800
Some felt as though the label didn't completely
fit, given how subjective and ill-defined

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:06.320
some people consider the term "sociopath"
to be.

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:10.460
Thus, fans did what most everyone does nowadays
when they need to blow off steam and have

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:14.960
their thoughts heard: they headed to Twitter
to air their grievances in true Festivus fashion.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:15.900
One wrote:

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.980
"Isn't Thanos a psychopath, not a sociopath?

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:21.400
Pls correct me if my dumbass is wrong."

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:22.620
Another had this to say:

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:26.380
"[...] does this mean that Thanos knows that
what he's doing is wrong, but is doing it

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:27.720
anyway because he's stubborn?

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:32.100
Does he truly believe that wiping half of
life from the universe is key to saving it?"

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:36.700
One Marvel fan was certain that Netflix royally
messed up in classifying Josh Brolin's Mad

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:41.539
Titan as a sociopath, tweeting, "Really take
issue with Netflix categorizing Thanos as

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:42.520
a sociopath.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:43.600
He's clearly not."

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:48.030
Of course, until we get Thanos on the couch,
it's difficult to say with absolute certainty

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:51.620
whether the Mad Titan has a diagnosable personality
disorder at all.

00:01:51.789 --> 00:01:56.560
To summarize the two disorders in a not-at-all
scientific way, the generally accepted difference

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:00.159
between psychopathy  and
sociopathy is that a psychopathic

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:03.280
individual will not feel empathy or have a
sense of morality.

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:08.340
Meanwhile, a sociopathic person, by contrast,
does have a sense of morality, having the

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:12.040
knowledge that a particular action is bad,
but going ahead and doing it anyway.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:15.620
But despite these differences, the two terms
are frequently conflated.

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:19.820
And because none of us at home can truly know
whether Thanos felt bad about eradicating

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:24.500
half the universe's population or if he knew
that it was wrong but still did it anyway,

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:29.140
it's not hard to see why some fans have confused
the alien megalomaniac for being more of a

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:32.460
remorseless psychopath than regret-refusing
sociopath.

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:33.900
Want to see more of this debate?

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:34.820
Of course you do!

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:36.000
Back to the Tweets:

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:40.860
"He's a far more dangerous villain than a
sociopath — he's obsessed with his own power,

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.600
and believes what he's doing is right."

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:44.240
Another fan responded, tweeting:

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:46.080
"That's actually a psychopath.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:50.560
Sociopaths can feel empathy and regret but
ignore it to achieve their goal.

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:53.020
Psychopathy is the absence of, or impaired,
empathy.

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:56.120
During the movie, Thanos did exhibit signs
of remorse.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:57.720
Especially when it came to Gamora.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:02:59.800
"A sociopath is what he is.

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:00.360
He cried.

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:01.440
He showed remorse.

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:04.480
People are confusing sociopathy with psychopathy.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:07.500
Psychopathy is the ABSENCE of remorse or empathy."

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:12.040
As tired as you probably are of this discussion,
imagine how everyone else on the internet

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:12.540
felt.

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:16.980
The result of the exhausting back-and-forth
between the tweeting armchair psychiatrists

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:21.180
was that many outlets on the Internet started
reporting that Netflix had actually changed

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:25.570
the description of the movie to remove the
word "sociopath," instead describing Thanos

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:26.680
as "Invader.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:27.280
Annihilator.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:28.600
So-called savior."

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:33.280
Of course, as of the making of this video,
opening up Infinity War on Netflix reveals

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:37.140
the same sociopathic language as ever — at
least for some users.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:41.560
It's unclear if these reports seem to indicate
that Netflix has slowly begun rolling out

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:45.680
a changed synopsis, or if some people are
just getting confused by the two descriptions

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:48.100
that Netflix includes on all of its movies.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:52.700
Just like the debate between whether Thanos
is a psychopath and sociopath, this question

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:54.620
is likewise pointless and frustrating.

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:58.880
It is, indeed, a truly perfect note to close
out the year of 2018.

